 threat from Frank.

123
00:04:40,728 --> 00:04:43,283
- I knew it, I knew it!

124
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,526
Just look at what I
found in Frank's closet

125
00:04:45,526 --> 00:04:47,494
behind his Jane West doll.

126
00:04:47,494 --> 00:04:48,874
Dynamite.

127
00:04:48,874 --> 00:04:50,669
Not that I was snooping.

128
00:04:50,669 --> 00:04:51,912
But if I didn't
 snoop, I wouldn't know

129
00:04:51,912 --> 00:04:54,294
what was going on
 in Frank's life.

130
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:57,676
All right, Mickey, I've got
 it taken care of down here.

131
00:04:57,676 --> 00:05:01,922
Why don't you take in Ed
 Wood's The Sinister Urge,

132
00:05:01,922 --> 00:05:05,408
with a short about
 personal hygiene.

133
00:05:05,408 --> 00:05:07,859
Watch and learn, stink bombs.

134
00:05:09,826 --> 00:05:11,552
- This one's got good heft.

135
00:05:11,552 --> 00:05:13,727
Well, anyway, call us if you
 need us, Clay, all right?

136
00:05:13,727 --> 00:05:15,315
- Well, Gypsy, I think Frank
 would be really understanding

137
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:18,041
if you return his pinking
 shears and got something else.

138
00:05:18,041 --> 00:05:19,284
[alarm sounding]
[shouting]

139
00:05:19,284 --> 00:05:22,011
- Oh, great, we've
 got movie sign!

140
00:05:35,507 --> 00:05:37,267
[lighthearted orchestral music]

141
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:38,890
[humming]

142
00:05:38,890 --> 00:05:41,479
- [Mike] Wendell Yeo, the
 cleanest man in Boston.

143
00:05:41,479 --> 00:05:44,758
- What, were these
 sold door to door?

144
00:05:44,758 --> 00:05:47,105
- [Tom] Join us, join us.

145
00:05:47,105 --> 00:05:48,658
- In the eighth grade.

146
00:05:48,658 --> 00:05:51,868
They want to choose a boy
 and a girl from this class

147
00:05:51,868 --> 00:05:53,698
to be in their assembly.

148
00:05:53,698 --> 00:05:54,768
- [Tom] Who wants
 to be sacrificed?

149
00:05:54,768 --> 00:05:56,114
- All right, put
your hands down.

150
00:05:56,114 --> 00:05:57,840
They'll have to choose.

151
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,256
- [Mike] The eighth-graders
 cull the herd.

152
00:06:00,256 --> 00:06:01,913
- [Narrator] Whomever
John and Arlene choose,

153
00:06:01,913 --> 00:06:03,535
you can be sure of one thing.

154
00:06:03,535 --> 00:06:05,986
It won't be anyone who
 isn't clean and neat.

155
00:06:05,986 --> 00:06:07,850
- [Crow] They'll sniff everyone.

156
00:06:07,850 --> 00:06:09,369
- [Narrator] Looking clean
 and neat is something

157
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:11,957
everyone is expected to do,
 and for a very good reason.

158
00:06:11,957 --> 00:06:13,373
- [Tom] Here's the
 shrooms, Billy.

159
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:14,581
- [Narrator] It's
 important to your health,

160
00:06:14,581 --> 00:06:17,135
and to the health
 of those around you.

161
00:06:17,135 --> 00:06:19,309
Don may feel that he
 looks neat enough.

162
00:06:19,309 --> 00:06:20,794
- But Don's wrong.

163
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:22,865
- [Narrator] But let's go
 back to the start of the day

164
00:06:22,865 --> 00:06:24,763
and see what we can do.

165
00:06:25,971 --> 00:06:28,353
There you are, Don, back
in bed this morning.

166
00:06:28,353 --> 00:06:29,837
- Now, a giant cockroach.

167
00:06:29,837 --> 00:06:31,667
- [Narrator] First of all,
 form the habit of getting up

168
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:32,840
in plenty of time.

169
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,290
- [Tom] To sober up.

170
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:35,809
- [Narrator] Keeping
 clean and neat is a matter

171
00:06:35,809 --> 00:06:38,432
of forming good habits and
 letting them work for you.

172
00:06:38,432 --> 00:06:40,986
- [Mike] Oh man, what the
 hell did I do last night?

173
00:06:40,986 --> 00:06:42,436
- [Narrator] Now, don't stall.

174
00:06:42,436 --> 00:06:44,231
If you lie in bed so long
 that you have to rush,

175
00:06:44,231 --> 00:06:46,475
how can you expect
 to be neat and clean?

176
00:06:46,475 --> 00:06:49,236
- Lay off, you're
 suffocating me!

177
00:06:50,548 --> 00:06:53,792
[humming "Psycho" theme]

178
00:06:53,792 --> 00:06:55,311
- [Tom] Psycho.

179
00:06:55,311 --> 00:06:56,312
- [Narrator] Or in winter,
 when you're hot and sweaty,

180
00:06:56,312 --> 00:06:57,900
every other day will do.

181
00:06:57,900 --> 00:07:00,799
Make it a shower or a
tub, whichever you like,

182
00:07:00,799 --> 00:07:02,318
