193
00:07:22,787 --> 00:07:23,926
- [Narrator] And keep a
fingernail brush handy

194
00:07:23,926 --> 00:07:25,203
for your nails.

195
00:07:25,203 --> 00:07:27,654
You're not clean if
your fingernails aren't.

196
00:07:27,654 --> 00:07:29,828
- [Mike] You are now officially
obsessive-compulsive.

197
00:07:29,828 --> 00:07:31,243
- [Narrator] Then
rinse all the soap off.

198
00:07:31,243 --> 00:07:32,797
- [Tom] Rinse,
 dammit, rinse, rinse!

199
00:07:32,797 --> 00:07:34,039
- [Narrator] Learn to make
 good habits work for you

200
00:07:34,039 --> 00:07:36,110
by following the same
 order every time.

201
00:07:36,110 --> 00:07:39,907
- So clean yourself
 in alphabetical order.

202
00:07:39,907 --> 00:07:42,945
- [Tom] Use pumice on
your tender nipple buds.

203
00:07:42,945 --> 00:07:44,187
- [Narrator] And
 here's another habit.

204
00:07:44,187 --> 00:07:47,052
Wash your hair on the
 same day each week.

205
00:07:47,052 --> 00:07:50,297
Tuesday, Wednesday, Saturday,
 whichever day you choose.

206
00:07:50,297 --> 00:07:52,817
- [Mike] Keep a
 detailed log, though.

207
00:07:52,817 --> 00:07:54,853
- [Narrator] Use a
 good shampoo or soap,

208
00:07:54,853 --> 00:07:56,752
and rub in the lather
 with your fingers,

209
00:07:56,752 --> 00:07:58,236
not your fingernails.

210
00:07:58,236 --> 00:07:59,893
- [Mike] Here, let me help you.

211
00:07:59,893 --> 00:08:02,309
- [Narrator] Lather up twice,
 with a rinse in between.

212
00:08:02,309 --> 00:08:03,793
- Why couldn't they
have had Mamie Van Doren

213
00:08:03,793 --> 00:08:05,381
star in this thing?

214
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:08,315
- [Narrator] And after
 the second lather,

215
00:08:08,315 --> 00:08:11,629
when your hair is perfectly
 clean, rinse again.

216
00:08:11,629 --> 00:08:14,459
Keep rinsing til every
 bit of soap is out.

217
00:08:14,459 --> 00:08:16,185
- [Tom] [imitating knocking]
 You almost done in there?

218
00:08:16,185 --> 00:08:17,773
What are you doing?

219
00:08:20,534 --> 00:08:22,053
[humming]

220
00:08:22,053 --> 00:08:22,916
- [Narrator] There.

221
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:24,193
Feels good, doesn't it?

222
00:08:24,193 --> 00:08:25,712
- [Tom] No no no,
 don't touch that.

223
00:08:25,712 --> 00:08:26,851
- [Narrator] Give yourself a
 good rubdown with the towel

224
00:08:26,851 --> 00:08:29,267
until you're completely dry.

225
00:08:29,267 --> 00:08:30,544
- [Mike] Please remain
seated until the shower

226
00:08:30,544 --> 00:08:32,408
has come to a full
 and complete stop.

227
00:08:32,408 --> 00:08:33,616
- [Narrator] Now, before
you brush your hair,

228
00:08:33,616 --> 00:08:35,722
be sure your comb
 and brush are clean.

229
00:08:35,722 --> 00:08:37,240
- He's becoming Howard Hughes!

230
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,863
- [Narrator] Wash them the
 day you wash your hair.

231
00:08:38,863 --> 00:08:42,694
- [Tom] Have an extensive
 filter system installed.

232
00:08:42,694 --> 00:08:45,317
- [Mike] Comb your
Darren Stevens haircut.

233
00:08:45,317 --> 00:08:46,146
- [Narrator] Your teeth--

234
00:08:46,146 --> 00:08:47,527
- [Tom] Comb them too.

235
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,874
- [Narrator] They're clean now.

236
00:08:49,874 --> 00:08:51,358
Brush them again
after breakfast,

237
00:08:51,358 --> 00:08:53,187
so they'll be clean
 again til lunch.

238
00:08:53,187 --> 00:08:55,362
- Aha, aha, mad dog, aha!

239
00:08:55,362 --> 00:08:57,640
- [Narrator] Before
you leave the bathroom,

240
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,883
- [Tom] Flush.

241
00:08:58,883 --> 00:09:00,712
- [Narrator] See that it
is neat and clean too.

242
00:09:00,712 --> 00:09:03,750
Towel and wash cloth
 hung up to dry.

243
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:06,097
Cap back on the shampoo.

244
00:09:06,097 --> 00:09:07,823
- [Mike] Dun-dun-dun!

245
00:09:07,823 --> 00:09:10,308
- [Narrator] Bathtub clean.

246
00:09:10,308 --> 00:09:11,654
Basin clean.

247
00:09:11,654 --> 00:09:13,656
- Pick up all the
 hairs with a tweezer.

248
00:09:13,656 --> 00:09:15,555
- [Narrator] Yes,
everything is put away.

